So, then, here's the updated list of bugs we
don't currently really know anything about.
Any information about what these bugs mean
or how to reproduce them would be helpful...

C341-5 When you see your pet move, the pet may be referred to as
"it".
C342-12 There are a number of places that misuse "your".
C343-1 At a pit the game can give messages with poor grammar.
C343-46 Breaking up a boulder or statue can result in pieces that are
described incorrectly.
C343-60 Several messages delivered when hero's fingers are slippery
have poor grammar.
C343-62 Riding into a magic portal gives an extra, useless message.
C343-75 Eating Medusa's corpse may not work properly.
C343-85 Sometimes the hero can't move when conscious.
C343-86 Hero can appear to be in the wall after destroying a
drawbridge.
C343-87 Sometimes shop items the hero is forced to buy can be sold
twice.
C343-92 A blind player may find a trap which then fails to show up on
the map.
C343-102 Messages delivered when the ceiling collapses on a swallowed
hero need revision.
C343-110 Game can crash if shopkeeper dies while character is
praying.
C343-112 Hero and monster afflicted with lycanthropy are treated
differently.
C343-133 Effects of varying consuming Medusa are inconsistent.
C343-143 Leprechauns stealing gold from a mounted hero cause oddly
worded messages.
C343-152 Using a cursed lamp while blind may give inappropriate
messages.
C343-162 Using Magicbane may cause an ungrammatical message.
C343-164 Cancelled nurses may give inappropriate messages.
C343-166 Pits dug in vault guard's corridor don't get removed.
C343-167 Length of time swallowed is sometimes calculated incorrectly.
C343-168 Shattering a monster's weapon doesn't work right if the
weapon is part of a stack of more than one.
C343-172 Crash could occur when monster uses potion or food to cure
stoning or confusion.
C343-173 Monster eating lizard corpse is not handled correctly.
C343-174 Drum of earthquake gives inappropriate message if hero or
monster is in a pit.
C343-177 First false rumor is displayed as gibberish on some
platforms.
C343-178 Wisdom is mishandled when rumors are used for random
graffiti.
C343-180 In an obscure case on special levels, troll corpses may fail
to revive and lizard corpses may revive.
C343-181 The hero is welcomed to Delphi even if the Oracle was
previously angered.
C343-182 Putting on the Eyes of the Overworld while blind gives an
ungrammatical message.
C343-185 No message is generated when attempting to name a monster
that cannot be named by the player.


